The '''Celanon Spur''' was a [[hyperspace route]] in [[the galaxy]] that ran from [[Dorin]] in the [[Mid Rim Territories]] to [[Celanon]], an astronomical object on the [[Hydian Way]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="Route" /> The [[Axxila–Tangrene hyperlane]]<ref name="Map">{{StarWarsGalaxyMap}}</ref> joined with the Celanon Spur.<ref name="BMF 48" />

The [[Pandem Nai system]], containing the [[planet]] [[Pandem Nai]], was located on the route.<ref name="Alphabet Squadron" /> The [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] planet [[Ord Mantell]] was also located on the route.<ref name="BMF 48" /> The [[gas giant]] [[Ajara]] and its [[moon]], the [[jungle]] world [[Ajan Kloss]], located in the [[Cademimu sector]] of the Outer Rim Territories, were situated in a partially unexplored stretch of [[Realspace|space]] off the Celanon Spur.<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

While preparing for an [[Battle of Pandem Nai|attack]] on the forces of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[204th Imperial Fighter Wing]], who had fortified themselves on Pandem Nai following the [[Battle of Endor]]<ref name="Alphabet Squadron" /> in [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> [[New Republic Intelligence]] [[agent]] [[Caern Adan]] studied the Celanon Spur. While the Celanon Spur would be an easier route to the planet, Adan presumed that the 204th would have placed early warning mechanisms along the hyperlane.<ref name="Alphabet Squadron" />

